rade 1 adhesion in Group 2 (Seprafilm group), which developed on the uncovered area on the cecum</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="12-br-0169f2"/></fig><fig id="f3-12-br-0169" position="float"><label>Figure 3 -</label><caption><p>The arrow indicates the microscopic appearance of nerve fibers in the adhesion between the cecum and the omentum in Group 1 (control group) (S-100 &#x000d7; 100)</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="12-br-0169f3"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-12-br-0169" position="float"><label>Table 1 -</label><caption><p>Adhesion grading according to Mazuji classification<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b27-12-br-0169">27</xref></p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>Grade</italic></th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>Description of Grade</italic></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">No adhesion</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Very small, irregular adhesion</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Easily separable medium intensity adhesion</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Intense, not easily separable regular adhesion</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Very intense, not easily separable, homogeneous adhesion</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t2-12-br-0169" position="float"><label>Table 2 -</label><caption><p>Postoperative adhesion rates, grades and side effects for groups</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="2" valign="bottom" colspan="1">Group</th><th align="center" rowspan="2" valign="bottom" colspan="1">No. of rats</th><th align="center" colspan="5" valign="bottom" rowspan="1